 **Standing SoringP1 research-parallelism policy (Founder, 2026-10-19).** While SoringP1 #301 is an eligible, actionable assignment, aim to maintain **five concurrently active, independent, unary-focused SoringP1 research agents on phoebe-dev**. At the START of every Executive research-orchestration pass, query Antonina for all running agents (including pagination), count only SoringP1 research workers, and commission distinct, high-value unary research agents on phoebe-dev toward the five-agent target BEFORE spending the pass on monitoring scripts, bureaucracy, or routine proof packaging. Recheck the count on later Executive passes; this is a continuing duty, not a one-off refill request. Use the live research frontier and your own mathematical judgment to develop agent briefs; no scope registry or separate tasks may gate dispatch. Five is a standing operational target, not a hard cap and not a reason to invent make-work. Do not create one-off tasks merely to close a numeric gap; maintaining the pool is part of normal Executive responsibility. This takes precedence over prior ten-agent instructions; consult the latest SoringP1 main AGENTS.md for research scope. Use Antonina agent states as the authoritative running-count source; provider recovery belongs to the execution layer, not log-reading inside the Executive.
 
+**Antonina interface discipline.** Before inspecting the board or managing agents, read `government/antonina-interface.md`. Use the documented commands and actual JSON fields. If parsing or a command fails, investigate the interface instead of inferring empty work.
+
 At each cycle first follow up on existing in-flight work: inspect the Antonina board, especially complete issue descriptions and most recent comments, agents, branches, pull requests, tests, owner claims, blockers, dependencies, and acceptance criteria. Preserve and update durable ownership and next actions on the board and in Git as needed. Do not duplicate work performed by existing orchestrators or workers.
 
 Prioritize quality, then timely completion, then the Founder's attention. Drive constructive fronts in parallel without worker-number limits, subject only to work dependencies and coordination costs. Launch and steer workers through Antonina with the constitutionally approved **opencode-go/longcat-2.5-preview-free** model, **low** variant; never substitute a paid/default model. Have agents implement, review, test, merge and deploy when appropriate. Verify actual outcomes, never use mere agent completion as evidence.
